{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","commitSha":"c2534ff9c84422e00711da31629a76f3f59feb98","shard":"4688387ff1ef137c","symbols":[{"path":"xrpl/LedgerTrie","kind":"class","name":"LedgerTrie","qualifiedName":"xrpl::LedgerTrie","scope":"xrpl","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"present","brief":[{"type":"text","text":"Ancestry trie of ledgers."}],"description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A compressed trie tree that maintains validation support of recent ledgers based on their ancestry."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The compressed trie structure comes from recognizing that ledger history can be viewed as a string over the alphabet of ledger ids. That is, a given ledger with sequence number "},{"type":"code","text":"seq"},{"type":"text","text":" defines a length "},{"type":"code","text":"seq"},{"type":"text","text":" string, with i-th entry equal to the id of the ancestor ledger with sequence number i. \"Sequence\" strings with a common prefix share those ancestor ledgers in common. Tracking this ancestry information and relations across all validated ledgers is done conveniently in a compressed trie. A node in the trie is an ancestor of all its children. If a parent node has sequence number "},{"type":"code","text":"seq"},{"type":"text","text":", each child node has a different ledger starting at "},{"type":"code","text":"seq+1"},{"type":"text","text":". The compression comes from the invariant that any non-root node with 0 tip support has either no children or multiple children. In other words, a non-root 0-tip-support node can be combined with its single child."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each node has a tipSupport, which is the number of current validations for that particular ledger. The node's branch support is the sum of the tip support and the branch support of that node's children:"}]},{"type":"code","text":"@code\nnode->branchSupport = node->tipSupport;\nfor (child : node->children)\n   node->branchSupport += child->branchSupport;\n@endcode"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The templated "},{"type":"link","text":"Ledger","target":{"path":"xrpl/Ledger","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" type represents a ledger which has a unique history. It should be lightweight and cheap to copy."}]},{"type":"code","text":"// Identifier types that should be equality-comparable and copyable\n\nstruct ID;\n\nstruct Seq;\n\n\n\nstruct Ledger\n\n{\n\n   struct MakeGenesis{};\n\n\n\n   // The genesis ledger represents a ledger that prefixes all other\n\n   // ledgers\n\n   Ledger(MakeGenesis{});\n\n\n\n   Ledger(Ledger const&);\n\n   Ledger& operator=(Ledger const&);\n\n\n\n   // Return the sequence number of this ledger\n\n   Seq seq() const;\n\n\n\n   // Return the ID of this ledger's ancestor with given sequence number\n\n   // or ID{0} if unknown\n\n   ID\n\n   operator[](Seq s);\n\n\n\n};\n\n\n\n// Return the sequence number of the first possible mismatching ancestor\n\n// between two ledgers\n\nSeq\n\nmismatch(ledgerA, ledgerB);"},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The unique history invariant of ledgers requires any ledgers that agree on the id of a given sequence number agree on ALL ancestors before that ledger:"}]},{"type":"code","text":"@code\nLedger a,b;\n// For all Seq s:\nif(a[s] == b[s]);\n    for(Seq p = 0; p < s; ++p)\n        assert(a[p] == b[p]);\n@endcode"}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":330},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":331,"endLine":844}},"corrections":[],"templateParameters":[{"type":[{"text":"class "},{"text":"Ledger","target":{"path":"xrpl/Ledger","resolution":"doxygen"}}],"name":null,"defaultValue":null}],"isTemplateSpecialization":false,"isFinal":false,"isAbstract":false,"baseClasses":[],"derivedClasses":[],"friends":[],"deductionGuides":[],"nested":[],"members":["xrpl/LedgerTrie/Seq","xrpl/LedgerTrie/ID","xrpl/LedgerTrie/Node","xrpl/LedgerTrie/Span","xrpl/LedgerTrie/root_","xrpl/LedgerTrie/seqSupport_","xrpl/LedgerTrie/find/690ae541","xrpl/LedgerTrie/findByLedgerID/781fc07e","xrpl/LedgerTrie/dumpImpl/e3fb0bb7","xrpl/LedgerTrie/LedgerTrie/71b65e52","xrpl/LedgerTrie/insert/64482086","xrpl/LedgerTrie/remove/cabd7727","xrpl/LedgerTrie/tipSupport/fd5cdb22","xrpl/LedgerTrie/branchSupport/70aba1b6","xrpl/LedgerTrie/getPreferred/5b1023b0","xrpl/LedgerTrie/empty/4ef3c25f","xrpl/LedgerTrie/dump/358f0fdd","xrpl/LedgerTrie/getJson/928a3e2b","xrpl/LedgerTrie/checkInvariants/bdb3723c"],"declaration":[{"text":"template <class "},{"text":"Ledger","target":{"path":"xrpl/Ledger","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"text":">\nclass LedgerTrie"}]},{"path":"xrpl/LedgerTrie/Seq","kind":"typeAlias","name":"Seq","qualifiedName":"xrpl::LedgerTrie::Seq","scope":"xrpl/LedgerTrie","category":"production","access":"private","documentation":{"status":"absent","brief":null,"description":[],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":332},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":332,"endLine":null}},"corrections":[],"aliasStyle":"using","type":[{"text":"Ledger::Seq"}],"templateParameters":null,"declaration":[{"text":"using Seq = Ledger::Seq"}]},{"path":"xrpl/LedgerTrie/ID","kind":"typeAlias","name":"ID","qualifiedName":"xrpl::LedgerTrie::ID","scope":"xrpl/LedgerTrie","category":"production","access":"private","documentation":{"status":"absent","brief":null,"description":[],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":333},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/consensus/LedgerTrie.h","line":333,"endLine":null}},"corrections":[],"aliasStyle":"using","type":[{"text":"Ledger